			"notes": "This update mainly fixes compatibility issues.\n\n# Bug Fixes\n* MultiMC support\n* Optifabric support\n* Previously incompatible mods are likely now compatible (with the exception of Immersive Portals)\n\n# Installation\nSame as before, make sure you have the latest version of Fabric installed and also the latest version of the Fabric API downloaded. Then, just download and copy the `fpv-racing-mod-0.1.3.jar` file into your mods folder. __Note:__ `fpv-racing-mod-0.1.3.jar` is the file you want unless you know what you're doing.\n\nIf you use a Taranis transmitter like me, you're all done and ready to fly. Otherwise, you will need to modify some values in the fpvracing.cfg file (e.g. throttle, pitch, roll, and yaw). Also, a set of commented out values is included in the config for PlayStation 4 controllers."
		},
