			"notes": "This is the third official release of the FPV Racing Mod which is mainly just a bug fix and quality of life update.\n\n# Features\n* Your hand now automatically switches to your transmitter item when goggles are activated\n* Cactuses and magma blocks now kill the drone upon contact\n\n# Bug Fixes\n* Fixed language issues with the config file\n\n# Installation\nSame as before, make sure you have the latest version of Fabric installed and also the latest version of the Fabric API downloaded. Then, just download and copy the `fpv-racing-mod-0.1.2.jar` file into your mods folder. __Note:__ `fpv-racing-mod-0.1.2.jar` is the file you want unless you know what you're doing.\n\nIf you use a Taranis transmitter like me, you're all done and ready to fly. Otherwise, you will need to modify some values in the fpvracing.cfg file (e.g. throttle, pitch, roll, and yaw). Also, a set of commented out values is included in the config for PlayStation 4 controllers."
		},
