			"notes": "This is the second official release of the FPV Racing Mod which is mainly just a bug fix and quality of life update.\n\n# Features\n* Player name tags above drones\n* EMP now only destroys your own drone\n* Drones can now be spawned using the /summon command\n\n# Bug Fixes\n* Server console no longer prints error messages about the config\n* Server console no longer prints \"[player] moved too quickly!\" repeatedly\n* Sound can now be heard while outside of the goggles\n* Yaw thrust is no longer dependent on the game's framerate\n\n# Installation\nSame as before, make sure you have the latest version of Fabric installed and also the latest version of the Fabric API downloaded. Then, just download and copy the `fpv-racing-mod-0.1.1.jar` file into your mods folder. __Note:__ `fpv-racing-mod-0.1.1.jar` is the file you want unless you know what you're doing.\n\nIf you use a Taranis transmitter like me, you're all done and ready to fly. Otherwise, you will need to modify some values in the fpvracing.cfg file (e.g. throttle, pitch, roll, and yaw). Also, a set of commented out values is included in the config for PlayStation 4 controllers."
